tape:

0 run? | 1 typed char | 2, 3 temps | 4 guard | 5+ buffer!

every command should start at like t3 around

explanations: 
t0      holds 1 when prompts shoudl keep going, 0 when it should stop
t1      holds user input
t2,3    temporary cells, used for comparing values without destroying them
t4      stays 0 forever, is boundary for where the buffer starts (the square brackets in brainfuck repeat until the selected pointer is 0, so you can loop all the way to this, zeroed, cell) 
t5      where read stores `line`, the newline in `line` also helpfully acts as a guard (t4-like) for any square bracket loops :D

